# 011 US3 — no page of Draft Genie may be framed.
#
# The app served NO frame protection at all: no X-Frame-Options, no CSP, nothing,
# confirmed against production. Any site could embed draft.neelamjai.com.
#
# That becomes an attack the moment US3 adds a one-click "enable the relay"
# button, because FR-018 requires that enabling cannot be triggered by a page the
# owner merely visits — and a framed button clicked through an overlay is exactly
# that. It also protects the magic-link confirmation, whose entire job is to let
# someone SEE which account they are signing into.
#
# Assets are served by the platform ahead of the Worker, so this cannot be a
# middleware; the sign-in confirmation sets the same headers itself because it IS
# a Worker response.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer

# 010 T012 — the userscript must never be served stale.
#
# FR-022's "fix in minutes" depends on the script manager fetching the current
# file when it checks @updateURL. A cached copy at the edge would silently pin
# the user to a broken version during a draft, which is exactly the failure the
# userscript delivery form was chosen to avoid.
/draft-tap.user.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
  Content-Type: text/javascript; charset=utf-8
